<!--
  The TUNER key's mark: `mapping`, from M ICON.

  TUNER is the MAPPING category's tool, and in TSUNAGI///M the category word IS
  the mark (tsunagi-m-release §3.2). What was here before was the ///M three-bar
  motif the tool used to ship as its favicon — a family mark rather than the one
  that says which of the six things this key opens.

  Geometry: the six quadrilaterals read out of `M ICON/icons/mapping-1024.png`,
  scaled to the 24-unit viewport the console icons use.

  ## One tone, so the accent cell is white

  The source mark lifts the third slit's upper cell in mapping orange #E24A1B.
  It is not reproduced. Every icon on this console is one flat tone that swaps
  between #FFFFFF by day and #C6C3BD at night (docs/04 §10.9); a two-colour mark
  here would be the only object on the fascia that disobeys that, which says
  more about the design system than it does about TUNER. The lifted cell still
  reads as lifted — it is displaced, not just recoloured.

  ## Why this is smaller than what it replaces

  The ink spans 77% of the viewport where the old ///M bars spanned 94%. That is
  deliberate: `mapping` and `monitoring` are drawn at ONE shared scale so their
  strokes match when the two keys sit side by side on this console, and
  tsunagi-m-release §4.1 is explicit that per-mark scaling breaks the family.
  `monitoring` is the wider mark, so it sets the scale and `mapping` comes out
  smaller than the bars it replaces.

  Filled with @color/d_icon rather than left untinted: ConsoleKeys.applyNight
  lays a SRC_IN filter over this at runtime, so the declared colour only matters
  before the first swap. Naming the same token keeps the two in step.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
    <!-- The lifted cell of the third slit: the one the source paints orange. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="@color/d_icon"
        android:pathData="M18.36 3.43 H21.2 L19.62 7.79 H16.78 Z" />
    <path
        android:fillColor="@color/d_icon"
        android:pathData="M8.26 5.46 H11.13 L7.46 15.62 H4.59 Z" />
    <path
        android:fillColor="@color/d_icon"
        android:pathData="M12.92 5.46 H15.82 L13.43 12 H10.57 Z" />
    <path
        android:fillColor="@color/d_icon"
        android:pathData="M16.46 8.62 H19.33 L14.99 20.57 H12.12 Z" />
    <path
        android:fillColor="@color/d_icon"
        android:pathData="M10.11 13.23 H12.98 L10.33 20.57 H7.46 Z" />
    <path
        android:fillColor="@color/d_icon"
        android:pathData="M4.14 16.85 H7 L5.67 20.57 H2.8 Z" />
</vector>
